late on September 16 and moved toward the Miller farm opposite Lee’s left"}]]}],["$","div","XII Corps-Maj. Gen. Joseph K. F. Mansfield",{"className":"command-entry","children":[["$","strong",null,{"children":"XII Corps"}],["$","span",null,{"children":"Maj. Gen. Joseph K. F. Mansfield"}],["$","small",null,{"children":"Followed I Corps across the upper creek late in the day to support the opening attack against the Confederate left"}]]}],["$","div","II Corps-Maj. Gen. Edwin V. Sumner",{"className":"command-entry","children":[["$","strong",null,{"children":"II Corps"}],["$","span",null,{"children":"Maj. Gen. Edwin V. Sumner"}],["$","small",null,{"children":"Concentrated east of the Antietam; the corps had camped on and around the Pry farm during the approach"}]]}],["$","div","V Corps-Maj. Gen. Fitz John Porter",{"className":"command-entry","children":[["$","strong",null,{"children":"V Corps"}],["$","span",null,{"children":"Maj. Gen. Fitz John Porter"}],["$","small",null,{"children":"Formed part of McClellan’s concentrated force and remained available near the army center and reserve"}]]}],["$","div","IX Corps-Brig. Gen. Jacob D. Cox",{"className":"command-entry","children":[["$","strong",null,{"children":"IX Corps"}],["$","span",null,{"children":"Brig. Gen. Jacob D. Cox"}],["$","small",null,{"children":"Exercised corps command after Jesse Reno’s mortal wound at South Mountain; waited east and southeast of the creek for the next day’s orders"}]]}],["$","div","VI Corps-Maj. Gen. William B. Franklin",{"className":"command-entry","children":[["$","strong",null,{"children":"VI Corps"}],["$","span",null,{"children":"Maj. Gen. William B. Franklin"}],["$","small",null,{"children":"Remained in Pleasant Valley to watch Harpers Ferry until McClellan ordered him toward Sharpsburg at 6 p.m."}]]}]]]}],["$","section","Confederacy",{"className":"command-column #9a3d32","children":[["$","h3",null,{"children":"Confederacy"}],[["$","div","Army of Northern Virginia-Gen. Robert E. Lee",{"c